<div class="mla-fields">{fields.map(([id,label,type,value,min,max,step])=><label>{label}<input id={'mla-'+id} type={type} value={value} min={min} max={max} step={step}/></label>)}</div>
<details><summary>Vector layout · import or edit</summary><p class="small">Rectangle array: stable id, x/y in µm from the back-left corner, w/h in µm, integer level 0–127. Overlap uses maximum gray level. Image rows increase toward machine front.</p><textarea id="mla-shapes" rows="9" aria-label="Vector pattern JSON"></textarea><label>Import job JSON<input id="mla-import" type="file" accept=".json,application/json"/></label><a href={base+'example-job.json'} download>Example input</a></details>
</section></div>
<section><div class="mla-head"><strong>03 / Latent exposure map</strong><span>SIMULATED · NOT MEASURED</span></div>
<div class="mla-maps"><figure><figcaption>Nominal pattern / commanded dose</figcaption><canvas id="mla-nominal" width="200" height="100"></canvas></figure><figure><figcaption>Stitched dose · dashed seam</figcaption><div class="mla-seam"><canvas id="mla-map" width="200" height="100"></canvas></div></figure></div>
<div class="mla-legend"><span class="mla-gradient" aria-hidden="true"></span><span id="mla-dose-scale" class="small">No result · dose scale unavailable</span></div><p id="mla-readout" aria-live="polite">No committed exposure yet.</p><p id="mla-probe" class="small">Move over dose map to inspect coordinates.</p>
<div class="mla-buttons"><button id="mla-export" disabled type="button">Export exposure revision JSON</button><button id="mla-csv" disabled type="button">Export dose CSV</button><a href={base+'example-exposure.json'} download>Example handoff</a><a href={base+'output-schema.json'} download>Output JSON schema</a><a href={base+'solver.mjs'} download>Numerical source</a></div>
<p class="small">Export schema bts.mla150.exposure.v1 preserves sample ID, parent and child revisions, layout IDs, field coordinates, dose units, nominal and actual arrays, and provenance. No development station adapter is claimed; example JSON documents the handoff.</p></section>
